Z||000000||rigdonhome||08-20-2001||07:33 PM||||Me again!<P>I'm new to Fieros and it seems like every time I post a question it sparks 2 or 3 more for me!<P>I bought my Fiero with full intentions of swapping in a V8 of some sort...  There seem to be some issues with the N* swap and the Fiero trannies, and possibly with the LT1 as well?  <P>Can anyone give me the gear ratios for the different Fiero trannies, both autos and sticks?  Also final drive ratios?  I'm a Front Engine/Rear Wheel Drive guy from way back and I'm not used to the transmission and rear end being one unit, so I wonder if the tranny has ratios for each gear and then a final multiplier similar to a rear differential gear ratio?  Or are all the gear ratios calculated with the final axle rpm in mind?  <P>I guess I should also be asking, is the transaxle designed as a combination of the traditional transmission mated to a traditional rear axle, or is the unit designed completely different, with gear ratios being adjusted so that a final 'rear end gear' ratio doesn't exist?  Does any of this make sense???<P>I need to take one apart!<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black<BR>5 speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Cherry!||||reg||6
Z||000001||DRH||08-21-2001||12:14 AM||||Transaxles basically combine the tranny and rear end into one unit. There is still a final drive ratio the only difference being that what would be the pinion and ring gears are parallel and mesh like traditional tranny gears. There is also a differential complete with traditional spider gears. <P>Here's a link to the ratios:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html</A>  <P>(Go to the bottom of the page and back to main index for a lot of other info)<P>Here's another link with a TON of links to Fiero info:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Happy browsing!||||reg||1
